# Tracer: the absolute value of a square needs a real base.
# Before (incorrectly accepted):
# abs(i^2) = i^2
# i^2 = -1
# abs(i^2) = -1
# 0 <= abs(i^2)
# 0 <= -1
# Former behavior: all five statements passed in strict mode.
# Now: the identity is available for a checked real base.
forall a R:
    abs(a^2) = a^2
abs((-2)^2) = (-2)^2
i^2 = -1
0 <= abs(i^2)
# Boundary: abs(i^2) = i^2 rejects because i is not real.
# Executable negative: abs_square_real_guard::complex_square_does_not_prove_negative_absolute_value.
# Evidence: target/release/litex -strict -lang en -f examples/proof_nodes/equal/by_builtin_rule/abs_square_real_base_guard.lit
